\f0\fs26 \cf2 A Memento client interacts with web resources by including an Accept-Datetime HTTP header that conveys its preferred datetime. The challenge for a Memento client is determining the Resource Type (https://mementoweb.org/guide/resourcetype/) of the resource it is currently interacting with (URI-Q): is it an Original Resource (URI-R), a TimeGate (URI-G), or a Memento (URI-M)?\
\
[INIT]\
\
SET URI-R=blank\
SET TimeGate-FLAG=FALSE\
\
===========\
\
[START]\
\
Issue an HTTP HEAD against URI-Q with an Accept-Datetime HTTP header and value that conveys the preferred datetime\
GOTO [TEST-0]\
\
===========\
\
[TEST-0]\
\
! \'97 Is URI-Q a TimeGate?\
\
IF (the response header from URI-Q contains "Vary: accept-datetime\'94) THEN\
	SET TimeGate-FLAG=TRUE\
ENDIF\
GOTO [TEST-1]\
\
============\
\
[TEST-1] \
\
! \'97 Is URI-Q a Memento?\
\
IF (the response header from URI-Q contains \'93Memento-Datetime:\'93) THEN\
	SET TimeGate-FLAG=FALSE\
	SET URI-R=blank\
		IF (the response status code from URI-Q is a 3XX) THEN\
			GOTO [FOLLOW]\
		ELSE\
			STOP !\'97 SUCCESS, you got a Memento\
		ENDIF\
ELSE\
	GOTO [TEST-2]\
ENDIF\
\
============\
\
[TEST-2]\
\
! Follow redirects\
\
IF (the response status code from URI-Q is a 3XX) THEN\
	GOTO [FOLLOW]\
ELSE\
	GOTO [TEST-3]\
ENDIF\
\
============\
\
[TEST-3]\
\
IF (TimeGate-FLAG=TRUE) AND (the response status code from URI-Q is a a 4XX or 5XX) THEN\
	We got a case of TimeGate error. How does the user agent handle this?\
ELSE\
	GOTO [TEST-4]\
ENDIF\
\
============\
\
[TEST-4]\
\
! It\'92s an Original Resource\
\
SET URI-R=URI-Q\
IF (the response header from URI-Q contains a \'93timegate\'94 link) THEN\
	SET URI-Q=the URI that is the target of the \'93timegate\'94 link\
ELSE\
	SET URI-Q=the URI of the user agent\'92s preferred TimeGate\
ENDIF\
GOTO [START]\
\
============\
\
[FOLLOW]\
\
URI-Q = the value of Location HTTP response header returned by URI-Q\
GOTO [START]\
}